&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The role is onsite, Monday to Friday, based in our offices at Buckingham Gate. It is essential we work at a fast pace and collaborate in person to create market-leading, unmatched events throughout the calendar year. It will be great to have you as part of our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Do you thrive in a fast-paced environment, where you gain a tremendous amount of responsibility? Do you want to be part of an exceptional entrepreneurial team with young, motivated and extremely driven people? And are you curious or passionate about people? If so, you might be our next Graduate Social Media Manager.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About us&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;CFO Insights is Northern Europe’s largest CFO forum and aims to connect and develop CFOs, finance leaders, and tomorrow&#39;s innovators by addressing the issues of the future CFO. We are connecting more than 11,000 professionals from more than 15 countries.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;CFO Insights is part of United Media (https://www.united-media.com/) which focuses on building large scale industry media and conferences products in sectors such as insurance, HR, private equity, retail, etc. As of today, we have organically launched 8 media companies and acquired one.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we offer you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;As our Graduate Social Media Manager you get the unique opportunity to take ownership of our content. You’ll be working in-person in your HQ in London where you will constantly be pushed out of your comfort zone. To ensure a never ending growth curve, we provide you with:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Opportunity of having a real impact - You’ll be getting operational experience in a start-up where both your work and the results are highly tangible and matter to the business.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Inspiration and guidance - A chance to work closely with our high performing team as well as with the CEO and founder of our company.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Unlimited growth potential in our company - we strongly believe in and have a track record of promoting internally.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Travel opportunity: You would be joining our conferences overseas.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Invaluable transferable skills - boost your interpersonal, research, organisation, outreach and project management skills through experience and training.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Your Responsibilities&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Responsibilities in this job will vary however, they will be mostly centred around:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Email marketing: Manage copywriting, graphics, strategy and optimisation for our newsletter, product updates and exclusive promotions.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Social media growth management: Manage and grow our LinkedIn - our largest channel to interact with our audience - and frequently test new content formats. We would also like you to help us leverage our content on YouTube and launch our Twitter.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Graphic design: You will be responsible for our visual identity across all of our marketing channels. We will make sure you’re equipped to do this in the best way possible.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Website: Design, SEO activities, UX optimisation. Work with us on improving and launching new formats that reflect our brand identity.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Analytics: To continuously measure and improve our performance metrics across channels. You will be working towards challenging targets and KPIs.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Paid advertising and PPC campaign management.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Synergy: To collaborate with the other departments to identify content worth sharing with our audience, and also to inform them of our brands’ progress.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;What we expect from you&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Please note that this job does not require any specific previous work experience as training is provided and we are looking to incorporate candidates across different levels of experience. However, we do require you to have a UK work permit. We also expect candidates to have obtained a bachelors or masters degree, or to be working towards obtaining university qualification.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Furthermore, we are looking for candidates who:&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Have a relentless drive and desire to be the very best at what they do;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Possess and unparalleled work ethic with a high sense of urgency;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Take ownership of everything they do, are proactive and follow through on commitments;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Are curious about people and love to speak, build and nurture relations;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Are an excellent communicator (especially) verbally and in writing;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Are well-organised and display the ability to structure and prioritise their work.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Startdate&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;Flexible&amp;nbsp;&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;span style=&quot;font-weight: 400;&quot;&gt;The role is onsite, Monday to Friday, based in our offices at Buckingham Gate. It is essential we work at a fast pace and collaborate in person to create market-leading, unmatched events throughout the calendar year. It will be great to have you as part of our team.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.co.uk">Jobs in United Kingdom</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is looking for a &lt;strong&gt;Wholesale Director EMEA &amp;amp; APAC&lt;/strong&gt; to join our &lt;strong&gt;Wholesale&lt;/strong&gt; team based in &lt;strong&gt;Paris&lt;/strong&gt;, covering a maternity leave.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a fixed-term contract (CDD), starting &lt;strong&gt;early December 2026&lt;/strong&gt; for the duration of the absence of the employee being replaced — expected to run through approximately &lt;strong&gt;May 2027&lt;/strong&gt;, with the exact end date depending on the return of the employee on leave. A structured handover is planned in two steps: an initial transition with the outgoing Director around mid-December 2026, and a second handover at the end of the assignment, around her return in May 2027.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;As a key contributor within our &lt;strong&gt;Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt; team, the Wholesale Director EMEA &amp;amp; APAC steps into an existing commercial organization and ensures continuity of leadership for our EMEA &amp;amp; APAC wholesale business during the interim period. The role directly manages a team of four — &lt;strong&gt;two Wholesale Managers EU + ME/APAC&lt;/strong&gt;, &lt;strong&gt;one ADV Manager EU&lt;/strong&gt;, and &lt;strong&gt;one Wholesale Support Intern&lt;/strong&gt; — and owns the commercial and operational performance of a multi-market portfolio operated through key accounts, agents, and franchise partners. The role also works closely with our &lt;strong&gt;Wholesale Strategic Advisor&lt;/strong&gt;, an internal resource who supports continuity throughout the assignment.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;This is a hybrid position based at our Paris HQ, with a preference for in-person work. The role reports to the &lt;strong&gt;CEO&lt;/strong&gt;.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Responsibilities Include:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Provide day-to-day leadership to the two Wholesale Managers EU + ME/APAC, the ADV Manager EU, and the Wholesale Support Intern, ensuring business continuity and uninterrupted decision-making during the interim period&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Own the commercial performance of the ME &amp;amp; APAC wholesale portfolio — sell-in, sell-through, forecasting, and seasonal budgets across key accounts, agents, distributors, and franchise partners&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Lead sell-in for any Paris showroom season(s) falling within the contract period: oversee collection presentation, negotiation, seasonal budgets, and payment terms with senior buyers&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Oversee the network of agents, distributors, and franchise / shop-in-shop partners across ME and APAC: targets, seasonal action plans, brand standards, and performance reviews&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Ensure ADV operational execution through the ADV Manager: order management, Key Account shipping compliance, 3PL coordination, and delivery / stocklist reporting&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Act as the primary escalation point for key accounts and priority partners in EMEA &amp;amp; APAC for the duration of the assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Partner closely with the Wholesale Strategic Advisor to ensure continuity on ongoing initiatives and institutional knowledge throughout the assignment&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Report portfolio performance directly to the CEO — sell-in/sell-out KPIs, budget vs. actuals, stock and delivery status&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Coordinate cross-functionally with Merchandising, Production, Operations, and Finance to secure deliveries and resolve escalations&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Maintain continuity on any in-flight strategic initiatives (including agent-to-direct market transitions) without introducing new strategic shifts absent CEO sign-off&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Complete a structured handover with the outgoing Director in mid-December 2026, and prepare a full handover back to her ahead of her return around May 2027&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Requirements:&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;8+ years of experience in fashion wholesale, including proven experience managing a commercial team across an international, multi-market portfolio&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong track record as Wholesale Director, Area Manager, or senior Wholesale Manager, with solid knowledge of &lt;strong&gt;EMEA markets&lt;/strong&gt;; working familiarity with APAC market dynamics is expected, as the region is operated through agents and distributors rather than direct management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Hands-on experience managing agents, distributors, franchise / master-franchise partners, and key accounts&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Strong command of sell-in / sell-out analysis, OTB logic, forecasting, and in-season performance management&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Experience overseeing a Sales Administration / Order Management function (ERP, 3PL coordination, key account portal compliance)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Proficiency with B2B and ERP tools (JOOR, NuOrder, Cegid Orli, NetSuite or equivalent) and advanced Excel&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Fluent English and French required&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;A confident, autonomous people manager, comfortable stepping into an existing team and reporting directly to executive leadership with minimal ramp-up time&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Available for a fixed-term assignment in Paris starting early December 2026, for the duration of the maternity leave&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Benefits &amp;amp; Perks&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;At ANINE BING Paris, we combine creative ambition with a people-first culture. Expect generous time off (including RTT), flexible work, exclusive discounts on our collections, and private sales access — so you can live the brand as much as you build it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Style Perks: Enjoy a generous employee discount and seasonal wardrobe allotments — so you can live the brand, not just represent it.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Base salary: commensurate with profile and experience.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Working at ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING seeks to empower its employees by providing an environment of mutual respect where equal employment opportunities are available to all applicants and teammates without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, disability, Veteran status, or other legally protected characteristics. Diversity and inclusion is critical to our success as a global brand, and we seek to recruit, develop, and retain the most talented people from a diverse candidate pool.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;More about ANINE BING&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;ANINE BING is a Los Angeles-based fashion house founded in 2012 that blends elements of Scandinavian simplicity with American energy to offer modern wardrobe essentials for women seeking a timeless yet rebellious approach to everyday style. Since its launch, ANINE BING has evolved into a global brand, available in over 90 countries with a growing network of brick-and-mortar retail stores in key cities worldwide.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Powered by a global team of over 250 employees, ANINE BING is headquartered in Los Angeles and Paris, with additional offices in New York and Shanghai.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;About Our Paris HQ&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Located just off the Champs-Élysées, our Paris headquarters at 1 Rue François 1er is a cornerstone of our international growth. As the home of our Product teams and other key functions, this space reflects our commitment to creativity, collaboration, and global perspective. As we continue to grow across Europe, our Paris office plays a central role in shaping the future of our brand.&lt;/p&gt;<p>Find more <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr/english-speaking-jobs">English Speaking Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Au cœur de l’entité Decathlon Digital, l&#39;équipe Data Platform recherche un·e Staff Software Engineer basé·e à Lille&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;.&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Pour accélérer la transformation de nos infrastructures et répondre aux enjeux d&#39;évolutivité, nous avons créé une équipe SWAT constituée d&#39;experts seniors et de Staff Engineers.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;En tant que &lt;strong&gt;Staff Software Engineer&lt;/strong&gt;, ta mission sera d&#39;apporter l&#39;excellence du génie logiciel sur l&#39;ensemble du périmètre de la Data Platform. Tu navigueras de manière transverse entre nos différentes équipes (Factory, Core Data Product - CDP, MLOps, Platform Engineering) pour poser les standards logiciels, concevoir les briques d&#39;infrastructure et garantir l&#39;excellence technique.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;TA FUTURE CONTRIBUTION&amp;nbsp;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Ce rôle est un track IC (&lt;em&gt;Individual Contributor&lt;/em&gt;) à fort impact : tu n&#39;as pas de management d&#39;équipe direct, mais un véritable rôle de leadership technique et de mentorat. En tant que Staff Software Engineer, tu seras le·la garant·e de l’excellence logicielle, de la robustesse de l&#39;écosystème et de l&#39;interopérabilité des plateformes.&lt;br&gt;Tu seras notamment en charge de :&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Excellence Software &amp;amp; Gouvernance des Applications Factory :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Tu standardises nos méthodes de software engineering pour l&#39;ensemble de la Data &amp;amp; AI Platform et t&#39;appuies sur les communautés d&#39;experts du digital Decathlon pour y diffuser les meilleures pratiques.&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Tu apportes un cadre logiciel rigoureux aux applications clés développées côté Factory, notamment ARC et le Data Contract Registry.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Outillage Platform &amp;amp; Integration Agentic :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Tu développes les briques logicielles complexes et exigeantes (APIs, SDKs internes, microservices) pour outiller les squads Data, MLOps et GenAI. Tu conçois l&#39;architecture technique assurant l&#39;interconnexion fluide, sécurisée et performante pour l&#39;agentic platform.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exposition des Données (Projet RACE):&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Tu apportes ton expertise d&#39;ingénierie logicielle sur le projet RACE, l&#39;offre stratégique de la Data Platform permettant de packager et déployer des APIs au-dessus du Datalake (couches Gold / Insight). Tu garantis la haute disponibilité, la sécurité et la scalabilité de ces APIs afin de fluidifier les usages opérationnels et applicatifs.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Exploration Temps Réel &amp;amp; Streaming :&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;strong&gt;&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;Fort·e de tes connaissances sur l&#39;écosystème Kafka / Streaming, tu explores et expérimentes de nouvelles architectures d&#39;Analytics Engineering en temps réel.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Gouvernance &amp;amp; FinOps :&lt;/strong&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;br&gt;Tu orientes les choix d&#39;architecture avec un réflexe FinOps fort, en optimisant continuellement les performances d&#39;exécution dbt / Databricks et les coûts d&#39;infrastructures associées.&amp;nbsp;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Qualité &amp;amp; Gestion de la Dette :&lt;br&gt;&lt;/strong&gt; Tu joues un rôle de sentinelle en identifiant de manière proactive la dette technique sur l&#39;ensemble de la Data Platform et en orchestrant son assainissement avec les équipes produit et ingénierie.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;STACK TECHNIQUE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Cloud AWS et GCP&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Databricks (Lakehouse, Delta Lake)&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Plateformes LLM Frameworks d&#39;Agents&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;MLFlow&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Airflow / Orchestration de données&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Terraform / Docker /&amp;nbsp;Kubernetes&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Kafka&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;h3&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE TU APPORTES&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/h3&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Leadership &amp;amp; Excellence Logicielle :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu as une solide expérience en génie logiciel et tu es passionné·e par les bonnes pratiques de développement (SOLID, TDD, Design Patterns, Modélisation).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Culture Platform Engineering :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu sais ce que signifie bâtir des &quot;produits pour les développeurs&quot; (APIs propres, documentation soignée, SDKs robustes).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Esprit Produit &amp;amp; FinOps :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu es orienté·e valeur métier, simplicité d&#39;usage pour les utilisateurs finaux et rentabilité des choix d&#39;architecture.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Pédagogie &amp;amp; Mentorat :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu aimes transmettre, former les équipes aux standards du software et faire monter en compétence les ingénieurs autour de toi.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Communication :&lt;/strong&gt; Excellent relationnel pour collaborer avec les MLOps, les PM et les équipes utilisatrices. Anglais fluide pour évoluer dans notre contexte international.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Expérience :&lt;/strong&gt; Tu justifies d’une solide expérience en tant que Senior ou Lead Software Engineer (ou Backend Engineer) avec une appétence forte pour les sujets de plateforme, d&#39;infrastructures cloud ou d&#39;outillage Data/IA.&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CE QUE NOUS T’OFFRONS&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;ul&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Organisation de travail hybride ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Matériel fourni en accord avec tes missions et nos engagements sociétaux (Mac ou Windows) ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Une équipe de projet locale au sein d&#39;un réseau mondial (possibilité de carrière internationale) ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Développement des compétences et accompagnement (diversité des projets, formations internes et externes, etc.) ;&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;li&gt;Package de rémunération (actionnariat salarié, bonus mensuels/trimestriels).&lt;/li&gt;
&lt;/ul&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;NOTRE ENGAGEMENT EN FAVEUR DE L&#39;INCLUSION ET DE L&#39;ACCESSIBILITE&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Chez Decathlon, nous reconnaissons l&#39;immense valeur qu&#39;apporte la diversité à nos équipes et nous nous efforçons continuellement de favoriser et de cultiver un lieu de travail inclusif et équitable : c&#39;est pourquoi l&#39;Inclusion est l&#39;un de nos Fondamentaux Humains. Nous encourageons les personnes de tous horizons et de toutes capacités à postuler, car nous sommes convaincu·es que la diversité des pensées, des cultures, des identités et des expériences vécues nous rend plus fort·es.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Decathlon s&#39;engage également à offrir un processus de sélection inclusif et accessible à tous les candidat·es. En cas de besoin d&#39;aménagement, tu peux en faire la demande via le formulaire de candidature, celle-ci sera confidentielle. Ces demandes n&#39;affectent pas le résultat du processus de recrutement&quot;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&amp;nbsp;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;div class=&quot;content-conclusion&quot;&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;DECATHLON DIGITAL&amp;nbsp;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;Imaginez si la technologie nous permettait de repousser les frontières et d&#39;offrir des expériences sportives inédites. C&#39;est précisément notre ambition chez Decathlon Digital ! Nous sommes une équipe de plus de 5 000 experts en ingénierie logicielle, gestion de produits, données, cloud et cybersécurité, répartis à Paris, Lille et Amsterdam. Ensemble, nous créons la plus vaste plateforme sportive numérique, en exploitant les innovations technologiques pour optimiser la chaîne de valeur, concevoir des expériences connectées et donner une seconde vie à nos produits.&lt;/p&gt;
&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;Changeons la donne pour de bon.&lt;/strong&gt; Notre passion du sport nous guide et nous voulons qu’elle perdure. C’est pourquoi nous nous engageons à bâtir un modèle technologique plus durable, en réduisant notre impact direct sur l&#39;environnement, et en créant un espace sûr et inclusif pour apprendre et nous épanouir ensemble. Rejoins l’équipe et façonnons le futur du sport.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;/div&gt;<p>Find <a href="https://www.arbeitnow.fr">Jobs in France</a> on Arbeitnow</a>

